NAME
    sh - execute bounded pipelines and streamed file redirection

SYNOPSIS
    COMMAND [ARG...] [< FILE] [> FILE | >> FILE]
    COMMAND... | COMMAND...

DESCRIPTION
    Single and double quotes group literal text; neither performs expansion.
    An unquoted | connects bounded byte streams. Unquoted < supplies the first
    stage from FILE. Unquoted > truncates or creates FILE before execution and
    streams final stdout, while >> creates or streams at the existing end.

    File streams use a 16 KiB default working buffer and are not capped by the
    shell. A failing command may leave an empty file or written prefix. The
    1 MiB limit applies only between sequential pipeline stages. Redirection
    paths do not enter command argv. Environment and variable expansion,
    stderr redirection, heredocs, jobs, and descriptor numbers are not supported.
